  "comments": "There are 1985 coins with a short date (far from pearls, left on picture) and long date (near to pearls, right) serif &#039;1&#039; in 1985.<br />\r\nIn both the coins shown on the picture from erdvilla there is no period following the G in G VICTORIA and the G is touching the pearls.<br /><br />\r\nIn the third variety (picture from TMS) the G in G. VICTORIA is followed by a period, it is separated from the pearls and the 5 has a coiled tail.<br /><br />\r\nThe first and second varieties, with &#039;G&#039; touching the pearls:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/55ad63db28188.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/55ad63db28188.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"103\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/650815b835603.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/650815b835603.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"100\" /></a><br />\r\n©erdvilla<br /><br />\r\nThe third variety, with &quot;G.&quot; separated from the pearls and with a period after the &quot;G&quot;:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62ddb1be24845.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62ddb1be24845.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n©TMS",
